{"accession":"PSI-39","acronym":"CFI","title":"Cool Flames Investigation","doi":"10.60555/m6pj-a914","psi_version":4,"license":"CC0-1.0","project_type":"Microgravity Investigation","flight_platform":"International Space Station (ISS)","hardware":"Multi-User Droplet Combustion Apparatus (MDCA), Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR)","research_area":"Combustion Science","sub_research_area":"Droplets","nasa_center":"Glenn Research Center (GRC)","start_date":"10-01-2020","end_date":"10-20-2021","release_date":"18-Sep-2024","objective":"The objectives of this investigation are to:\n 1) Examine the combustion behavior of n-dodecane and mixtures of n-dodecane/iso-dodecane at pressures ranging from 0.25 atm to 5 atm.\n 2) Analyze the effects of helium dilution on cool flame behavior.\n 3) Examine the behavior of combustion characteristics.\n 4) Investigate the relationship between droplet size, pressure, and flame extinction, and (5) understand the consequence of soot formation during cool flame combustion.","approach":"The Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) contains the Multi-User Droplet Combustion Apparatus (MDCA) which facilitates the controlled combustion of fuel droplets. A system of gas bottles and fuel syringes delivers the desired gas mixture to the combustion chamber ranging from 0.25 to 0.5 atm. Droplets of fuel are dispensed and suspended between hypodermic needles or tethered using silicon-carbide fibers. A hot-wire igniter is positioned near the droplet for ignition. After ignition the wire is retracted. Fuels observed include n-dodecane, farnesane, and mixtures of n-dodecane/iso-dodecane. Fuels diluted with molecular oxygen, atomic nitrogen, and helium to study the influence on flame extinction and dynamics. Flames were observed with a black-and-white camera for droplet size measurements. A UV camera was used for capturing the OH* radical emissions and flame size. Other high resolution cameras were used for monitoring and documentation. Narrow-band and wide-band radiometers for analyzed flame radiation.","hypothesis":"Flame combustion of liquid hydrocarbon fuels such as n-dodecane, n-dodecane/iso-dodecane mixtures, and faresane in microgravity can provide insights into low-temperature chemical kinetics, revealing critical parameters like droplet extinction diameters and flame dynamics that are not observable on Earth.","research_impacts":"A basic understanding of cool flames is important for understanding ignition phenomena of practical fuels and fuel additives. Cool flames play a key role in the development and selection of new fuels and the design of advanced engines such as clean, high-efficiency Homogeneous Charge Compression Ignition (HCCI) engines. The research will also help combustion chemists to develop new computational models to compute combustion performance in for many practical applications on earth, including an understanding of how cool flame reactivity determines octane and cetane number for fuels in spark ignition and diesel engines.\nCool Flames Investigation (CFI) will provide critical validation for complex chemical kinetic mechanisms, advance the understanding of flame dynamics and instabilities in low-temperature combustion, and support the design of safer spacecraft systems by refining knowledge of combustion in microgravity environments.","related":["PSI-69"],"in_scope":true,"scope_note":null,"family":"FLEX","fuel_phases":["liquid"],"configuration":"n-dodecane / iso-dodecane droplets","scale":"droplet (mm)","pillars":["suppression"],"needs":{"extinction":0.5},"key_variables":["pressure (0.5\u20135 atm)","O2","helium dilution","fuel mixture"],"sensors":["cameras"],"uses_data_from":[],"summary":"Cool-flame behaviour of dodecane droplets versus pressure and helium dilution, including extinction diameters.","file_categories":{"metadata":{"n":1,"bytes":10237,"examples":["PSI-39_metadata_PSI-118_CFI.zip"]},"Raw Data":{"n":2791,"bytes":718852964195,"examples":["PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_HIBMS_Camera_Settings.txt","PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_HIBMS_CFI_Camera_Settings.txt","PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_INTNS_Camera_Settings.txt","PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_MDCA_CFI_Testpoint_Settings.txt","PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_MDCA_Color_Camera_Settings.txt","PSI-39_Raw Data_F173E01_Radiometer_Readings.txt"]},"Analyzed Data":{"n":32,"bytes":13614684,"examples":["PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1261_Summary_prelim.pdf","PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1261_Summary.pdf","PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1239_Summary.pdf","PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1239_Summary_v2.pdf","PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1253_Summary.pdf","PSI-39_Analyzed Data_FLEX-1238_Summary.pdf"]},"Reports":{"n":1,"bytes":811459,"examples":["PSI-39_Reports_CFI Science Final Report.pdf"]},"Engineering Documents":{"n":1,"bytes":115496,"examples":["PSI-39_Engineering Documents_CFI Operational Requirements and Protocols.pdf"]},"Science Documents":{"n":3,"bytes":16099538,"examples":["PSI-39_Science Documents_CFI_DataSummary_Spreadsheet_Jan2021.xlsx","PSI-39_Science Documents_SRD_CFI.pdf","PSI-39_Science Documents_CFI_SCR.pdf"]},"Presentations":{"n":2,"bytes":5945283,"examples":["PSI-39_Presentations_Cool Flames in Space, a Hot Prospect on Earth_CFI.pdf","PSI-39_Presentations_Aspects of Cool-Flame Supported Droplet Combustion in Microgravity_CFI.pdf"]}},"total_file_bytes":718889568684,"contacts":[{"name":"Frederick Dryer","affiliation":"Princeton University","roles":["Co-Investigator (Co-I)"]},{"name":"Daniel Dietrich","affiliation":"NASA GRC","roles":["Project Scientist"]},{"name":"Tanvir Farouk","affiliation":"University of South Carolina","roles":["Co-Investigator (Co-I)"]},{"name":"Vedha Nayagam","affiliation":"Case Western University","roles":["Co-Investigator (Co-I)"]},{"name":"Forman Williams","affiliation":"University of California, San Diego","roles":["Principal Investigator (PI)"]}],"psi_url":"https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-39","profile":{"n_tests":87,"n_records":87,"record_types":{"test":87},"fuel_phases":["liquid"],"ranges":{"o2_mole_frac":[0.17,0.21],"pressure_kpa":[50.663,506.625],"he_mole_frac":[0.0,0.59]},"coverage":{"o2_mole_frac":87,"pressure_kpa":87,"he_mole_frac":87},"measured_quantities":[{"quantity":"n2_mole_frac","n":87}],"outcome_classes":{}},"publications":[{"title":"Can cool flames support quasi-steady alkane droplet burning?","authors":"V Nayagam, DL Dietrich, PV Ferkul, MC Hicks, FA Williams","doi":"10.1016/j.combustflame.2012.07.012"},{"title":"Cool-flame extinction during n-alkane droplet combustion in microgravity","authors":"V Nayagam, DL Dietrich, MC Hicks, FA Williams","doi":"10.1016/j.combustflame.2015.01.012"},{"title":"Partial-Burning Regime for Quasi-Steady Droplet Combustion Supported by Cool Flames","authors":"Nayagam Vedha, Dietrich Daniel L., Williams Forman A.","doi":"10.2514/1.J054437"},{"title":"The role of cool-flame chemistry in quasi-steady combustion and extinction of n-heptane droplets","authors":"Paczko Guenter, Peters Norbert, Seshadri Kalyanasundaram, Williams Forman Arthur","doi":"10.1080/13647830.2014.934296"},{"title":"Asymptotic analysis of quasi-steady n-heptane droplet combustion supported by cool-flame chemistry","authors":"Seshadri Kalyanasundaram, Peters Norbert, Williams Forman A., Nayagam Vedha, Paczko Guenter","doi":"10.1080/13647830.2016.1248494"},{"title":"Science in Short: Cool Flames","authors":"Rachel Barry","doi":""},{"title":"Low Temperature n-Dodecane Droplet Combustion Experiments Aboard the International Space Station","authors":"Dietrich Daniel, Krause Timmothy, Nayagam Vedha, Farouk Tanvir, Dryer Frederick, Williams Forman","doi":"10.1007/s12217-024-10115-x"}],"insights":[{"id":"cool-flames-low-temperature","need":"extinction","pillar":"suppression","title":"Cool flames: combustion at 500\u20131000 K","observation":"Cool diffusion flames have peak temperatures of about 500\u20131000 K. FLEX, CFI and CFI-G studied them on droplets and burners in microgravity.","conditions":"CFI-G (PSI-159), CFI (PSI-39), FLEX (PSI-69): hydrocarbon fuels, 0.5\u20135 atm.","design_question":"Could low-temperature reaction zones persist after visible flame extinction, and would optical or heat detectors see them?","limitation":"Research fuels and configurations; relevance to cabin fires is an open question, not a finding.","next_validation":"Check whether cabin-relevant fuels can sustain cool-flame chemistry in exploration atmospheres.","sources":[{"accession":"PSI-159","field":"researchImpacts"},{"accession":"PSI-39","field":"objective"},{"accession":"PSI-117","field":"objective"}],"evidence_kind":"psi_text"}],"variation":{"varied":[{"variable":"Fuel / sample","n_levels":3,"examples":["C12H26","[.75]/[.25] C12H26/iso-dodecane","[.60]/[.40] C12H26/iso-dodecane"]},{"variable":"Configuration","n_levels":2,"examples":["droplet (free)","droplet on fiber"]},{"variable":"O2 mole fraction","n_levels":2,"min":0.17,"max":0.21},{"variable":"Pressure (kPa)","n_levels":7,"min":50.663,"max":506.625},{"variable":"Diluent","n_levels":2,"examples":["N2 only","He+N2"]}],"fixed":[{"variable":"Material","value":"n-dodecane / iso-dodecane"}],"not_reported":["Thickness (mm)","Flow (cm/s)","Flow direction"]},"test_preview":[{"test_id":"PSI-39:CFI:0000","accession":"PSI-39","record_type":"test","source_file":"PSI-39_Experimental table_CFI.csv","source_row":2,"label":"Test 1206","test_date":"9-Mar-17","fuel":"C12H26","fuel_phase":"liquid","material_class":"n-dodecane / iso-dodecane","configuration":"droplet (free)","thickness_mm":null,"o2_mole_frac":0.21,"pressure_kpa":101.325,"flow_cm_s":null,"flow_direction":null,"diluent":"N2 only","co2_mole_frac":null,"he_mole_frac":0.0,"gravity":"microgravity","outcome":null,"outcome_class":null,"quality":[],"notes":null,"raw":{"Flex Number":"1206","Test Date":"9-Mar-17","Local Time":"02:03:08 pm est","CIR":"f068a03","Pressure":"1 atm","Oxygen":"0.21","Nitrogen":"0.79","Helium":"0","Fiber":"No","Fuel":"C12H26"}},{"test_id":"PSI-39:CFI:0001","accession":"PSI-39","record_type":"test","source_